From: keks2293 <rusik2293@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: ignore a static dr_mode=host when usb-role-switch is present

In `linux usb` boot mode the bootloader unconditionally adds a
dr_mode = "host" property to the device tree in RAM before handing off to
the kernel. That forces the DWC3 controller into HOST mode from probe, so
xhci-hcd is probed immediately and the first root-hub scan fires before the
charger_pd PDR indication. On a pre-plugged drive that early scan is absorbed
(the charger path is still in standby waiting for the charger type), so the
drive is never enumerated.

A static dr_mode=host contradicts a device that declares a dynamic
usb-role-switch: on such a controller the TYPE-C state machine (UCSI) must
decide the role, not a fixed property. When both are present, demote the
forced HOST to OTG so the role-switch/UCSI path takes over and the host
controller is created only after the role flips, i.e. after the PDR. This
reproduces the behavior of a normal (non-overlay) boot, which enumerates a
pre-plugged drive on its first scan.

On a normal boot there is no dr_mode property, so dwc->dr_mode is already
OTG and this change is a no-op; it only alters the bootloader-overlay case.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -56,6 +56,19 @@
 	struct device *dev = dwc->dev;
 	unsigned int hw_mode;
 
+	/*
+	 * A static dr_mode=host (e.g. forced by the bootloader) contradicts a
+	 * dynamic usb-role-switch. When the controller declares a role switch,
+	 * the TYPE-C state machine must decide the role, not a fixed property.
+	 * Demote to OTG so the role-switch/UCSI path can take over.
+	 */
+	if (dwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST &&
+	    device_property_read_bool(dev, "usb-role-switch")) {
+		dev_warn(dev,
+			 "dr_mode=host ignored: usb-role-switch present, using OTG\n");
+		dwc->dr_mode = USB_DR_MODE_OTG;
+	}
+
 	if (dwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_UNKNOWN)
 		dwc->dr_mode = USB_DR_MODE_OTG;
 
